  "text_input": "Patient is a 60-year-old female who presented with generalized weakness, vomiting (7-8 episodes), and fever for one day. She is a known case of Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus for 10 years and Systemic Hypertension. Clinical examination and investigations led to a diagnosis of acute gastritis, systemic hypertension, type 2 diabetes mellitus, and herpes labialis. 2D Echo revealed mild concentric left ventricular hypertrophy, sclerotic aortic valve, mild mitral regurgitation, and LV diastolic dysfunction with a normal ejection fraction of 58%. Laboratory tests showed a total bilirubin of 0.5 mg/dL and serum albumin of 3.7 g/dL. She was treated with antibiotics (Inj. Sporizox-S), insulin (Inj. Mixtard), and anti-emetics. Her symptoms resolved, and she was discharged with advice to continue her diabetic and hypertensive medications.",
